# Recorded input for the context menu example page (widgets/contextmenu.zig, `Example`), at
# 800 x 600 in the default theme: the canvas at x 8..308, y 34..194. Opened at (150, 100), the
# list is at x 150..231, y 100..224: Cut (y 103..133), Copy (133..162), Paste (162..192),
# Arrange (192..221), x 153..228; Arrange's submenu at x 231..320, y 189..254: To front
# (y 192..222), To back (222..251), x 234..317. One line per frame says what it does (format:
# input.Replay). Keys are USB HID: 81 Down, 79 Right, 101 the context-menu key, 41 Escape.
# 0: rest
frame
viewport 800 600
dt 0.016
pointer 400 300
# 1: secondary press on the canvas: the menu opens at the pointer, Cut highlighted
frame
pointer 150 100
buttons right
# 2: release it
frame
buttons
# 3: the pointer reaches Copy
frame
pointer 190 147
# 4: Down: Paste
frame
press 81
# 5: Down: Arrange
frame
press 81
# 6: Right: its submenu
frame
press 79
# 7: the pointer reaches To back
frame
pointer 275 236
# 8: press it
frame
buttons left
# 9: release: To back chosen, the menu closes
frame
buttons
# 10: the context-menu key: opens at the canvas's corner
frame
press 101
# 11: Escape: closed
frame
press 41
